    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.16) standing as our primary offensive anchors. Both benefit immensely from the matchup against Mor\u00e1n, whose 4.52 xERA and handedness alignment provide a clear path for exploitation. **Trea Turner** earns the day's top score by combining a prime leadoff spot with a +7% park factor, while **Kyle Schwarber**\u2019s elite xwOBA (0.399) makes him a high-leverage start despite the inherent variance in his profile. Further down the order, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.04) serves as a sneaky efficiency play; his +14% dynamic platoon edge against Holmes helps mitigate the penalty of the #9 spot, keeping him well within the \"Strong\" start tier as we prioritize his speed in our quest to dominate the scarcity of stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision today involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 50.86 score. While he remains a serviceable utility option, the optimizer favored the platoon advantages of **Kazuma Okamoto** (59.25) and the raw power output of **Yordan Alvarez** (64.92) to maximize our total base production against their respective starters. Conversely, we are keeping **Caleb Durbin** (40.85) on the bench; while his speed is vital to our organizational goals, the matchup against Wheeler is a significant hurdle, as the pitcher's elite skill and ability to hold runners (50% SB suppression) dragged **Caleb Durbin**\u2019s score near our floor. We will monitor the status of **Casey Schmitt** and **Dillon Dingler** closely; the former remains a high-variance asset while awaiting a confirmed lineup, but **Dillon Dingler** has been relegated to the bench indefinitely after failing to meet our 40.0 efficiency threshold today.",
